{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cm rod is built from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods. All of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods must come first, and are followed by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods. For example, the rod could be made from seven <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods followed by eight <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods. How many ways are there to build the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cm rod?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af94bd62af43ca7a04464edd2014abec7ffeb0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 5\\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm rods. The length must sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cm, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32220d211836a655baa463967e45e00682e148e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 2y = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b3f52e202c45bb68ec3b8166f71afdf62c5ba77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 11 = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but also must be odd because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> was even, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cab3f0704de3232f601b03d02a45d46103c172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> would be even and wouldn't be able to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad89ed6de49d089fcce622aa3dd3867c83445d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> different ways to build the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cm rod.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redli